SUMMARY:Nov 9 - Agentic Labeling for Specialized Visual Data
DESCRIPTION:Raleigh AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\n**Da
 te\, Time and Location**\n\nNov 09\, 2026\n9:00 AM - 10:00 AM PST\nOnline.
  **[Register for the Zoom!](https://voxel51.com/events/when-prompting-beat
 s-training-agentic-labeling-for-specialized-visual-data-november-9-2026)**
 \n\nFrontier multimodal models handle familiar concepts well and struggle 
 on niche ones: sorting drill-core samples into 35 geological classes\, or 
 telling adhesion from scarring on a ceramic substrate. Our study across 11
  specialized visual datasets in manufacturing inspection\, geology\, and m
 edical imaging found that a few labeled examples in the prompt can close m
 uch of that gap\, and it also found where that stops working.\n\n**What yo
 u’ll learn:**\n\n* Niche versus hard: how in-context examples supply dom
 ain knowledge a model is missing\, and how to tell a niche task from a gen
 uinely hard one\n* What the study measured: on an industrial defect task\,
  one labeled example per class raised macro-F1 from 34% to 59% with no fin
 e-tuning\, while on other tasks trained specialists pulled ahead at 5 to 1
 0 examples per class\n* Building a few-shot labeling task: define classes\
 , pick reference examples\, preview predictions on a small batch\, and ref
 ine the instructions\n* Finding the crossover point: when to stop promptin
 g a foundation model and train a specialist on bootstrapped labels\n* Runn
 ing it on your own data: attendees get free GPU compute from Nebius to try
  the workflow after the session
